1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,644
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,644 --> 00:00:09,940
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:03,698
<i>Get to the point before security takes you away
and you lose your chance forever.</i>

5
00:01:03,698 --> 00:01:06,066
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

6
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:08,488
<i>Dao, did you get to meet the chairman?</i>

7
00:01:08,488 --> 00:01:10,288
<i>I never thought I'd see her again.</i>

8
00:01:10,288 --> 00:01:12,460
<i>What does she want, Auntie?</i>

9
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,280
<i>Meeting like this...</i>

10
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:16,355
<i>if it isn't destiny, then what is?</i>

11
00:01:16,355 --> 00:01:19,480
<i>Do you have feelings for my sister?
You keep staring at her.</i>

12
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,560
<i>Dao.</i>

13
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,040
<i>What job was it again?</i>

14
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,120
<i>No, I'm not interested.</i>

15
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,240
<i>Mom!</i>

16
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:27,843
<i>Mom.</i>

17
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,500
[Operating Room]

18
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:48,180
Is it so bad that she needs surgery?

19
00:01:49,506 --> 00:01:52,200
They need to remove a blood clot in her heart.

20
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,800
Luckily, it's only a small one; otherwise...

21
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:01,846
Wait a minute.

22
00:02:01,846 --> 00:02:04,860
Why aren't you at work today?

23
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:07,680
Weren't you also sick the other day?

24
00:02:10,888 --> 00:02:12,085
Could it be...

25
00:02:12,085 --> 00:02:13,977
You got fired?!

26
00:02:22,911 --> 00:02:24,622
What are you both staring at?

27
00:02:24,622 --> 00:02:25,680
For lottery numbers.

28
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:28,040
You'll have to apply powder,
then rub it on her.

29
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,440
I'm not a tree spirit.

30
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,600
Is this the time to joke around?

31
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,330
I don't want you to stress out.

32
00:02:33,330 --> 00:02:34,755
Me neither.

33
00:02:34,755 --> 00:02:36,200
Hey, don't copy me.

34
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,155
Did you trademark it?

35
00:02:38,155 --> 00:02:39,266
Smart mouth!

36
00:02:39,266 --> 00:02:40,377
What about it?

37
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,866
I won't be unemployed for long.

38
00:02:45,866 --> 00:02:47,500
I'll find a new job soon.

39
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,640
I have some savings. I'm not stressed.

40
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,040
We should focus on Mom's condition for now.

41
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,440
You're not just stressed,

42
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:57,000
but you're super stressed.

43
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,460
Yeah.

44
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,281
I'd better wait for Mom.

45
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:05,120
- Wait.
- What?

46
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:08,240
Don't be childish and stress Ran out. Got it?

47
00:03:08,887 --> 00:03:10,130
Tell that to yourself.

48
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:14,377
You should prioritize taking care of Mom
over talking to your girlfriend. Got it?

49
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:22,080
Yeah, finish it quickly,

50
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:25,225
so he can sit comfortably

51
00:03:25,225 --> 00:03:27,960
and stargaze tonight.

52
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,426
Yes, ma'am.

53
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,289
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

54
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:40,400
It's your mother right here, not a ghost!

55
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,511
But I think it is.

56
00:03:42,511 --> 00:03:44,280
That's the right spot to hang it.

57
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:47,125
If you say so, I'll have to agree.

58
00:03:47,125 --> 00:03:50,175
Do you think I'm a dictator?

59
00:03:50,175 --> 00:03:52,360
Of course not.

60
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,200
I must sincerely admit, ma'am,

61
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:57,300
that your eye for things has never failed you.

62
00:03:58,511 --> 00:04:00,602
Why didn't my child or my grandchildren

63
00:04:00,602 --> 00:04:03,418
inherit it from me at all?

64
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,180
[28 years ago]

65
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,888
<i>How old are you?</i>

66
00:04:12,888 --> 00:04:15,111
<i>- I'm eight--
- He's eight years old.</i>

67
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:18,955
<i>He's also as handsome as his father.</i>

68
00:04:18,955 --> 00:04:21,520
<i>He's a good student and very smart,</i>

69
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:23,800
<i>just like his father.</i>

70
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,880
<i>Just be yourself.</i>

71
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:28,500
<i>I'm not a beauty pageant judge.</i>

72
00:04:32,022 --> 00:04:34,113
<i>Your first wife just died during childbirth.</i>

73
00:04:34,113 --> 00:04:36,320
<i>I'm his actual first wife.</i>

74
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,280
<i>I was here first,</i>

75
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,020
<i>but we just weren't legally registered.</i>

76
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,280
<i>No wonder.</i>

77
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,800
<i>You named your son "Lek,"</i>

78
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,560
<i>because you already have "Yai."</i>

79
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,820
<i>How dare you hide this from me?!</i>

80
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,580
<i>I apologize, Mother.</i>

81
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:57,720
<i>I...</i>

82
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,060
<i>I must also apologize.</i>

83
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,100
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

84
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,580
<i>It wasn't either of your faults.</i>

85
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,060
<i>It was my son's fault</i>

86
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,880
<i>for being a coward</i>

87
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,860
<i>who wasn't brave enough to tell the truth!</i>

88
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:15,016
<i>Had I known you already had a family,</i>

89
00:05:15,016 --> 00:05:17,539
<i>I wouldn't have let you marry Lek's mother.</i>

90
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,240
Hey.

91
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,977
Do you think my son's and Lek's mother's souls

92
00:05:35,977 --> 00:05:38,422
would fight if they met?

93
00:05:38,422 --> 00:05:40,640
I don't know. I've never died before.

94
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,644
Right!

95
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:45,644
No matter where they are,

96
00:05:45,644 --> 00:05:49,020
their souls must be resting peacefully by now.

97
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:52,060
That's true.

98
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,540
It's people like us who are still here.

99
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:01,040
I want to make sure
I have no worries left before I die,

100
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:04,200
so when I do, I can go to a better place.

101
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,711
That way, my spirit
won't have to remain in this house

102
00:06:06,711 --> 00:06:08,620
to watch over my descendants.

103
00:06:11,050 --> 00:06:13,360
I'm worried about them,

104
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,116
both Yai and Lek.

105
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:18,177
Yes.

106
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,461
You made me wait for so long.

107
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,080
Had I talked to you downstairs,

108
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:26,560
you would've cut me off and gotten up here.

109
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:28,760
That's why I'm waiting for you here,

110
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,540
so you can't walk away from me.

111
00:06:32,106 --> 00:06:34,069
I can walk out the door, Mom.

112
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,488
Just say what you want to say, Mom.

113
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,140
I want to talk about Daran.

114
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,844
What does she have to do with me?

115
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,844
I knew I was right.

116
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:52,860
How much money
did that wicked woman ask you for?!

117
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:54,500
Did you give it to her?

118
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,820
Don't make me think

119
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,920
you've really become a moron.

120
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,044
Mom.

121
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,720
Don't put me down.

122
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,120
I learn from my mistakes.

123
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:09,960
- Then why was she at the station?!
- I don't know!

124
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:13,600
Ever since I came back from abroad
and inherited the title from Father,

125
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:16,670
I've never contacted her,
met her, or even spoken to her.

126
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,145
I don't believe that!

127
00:07:19,145 --> 00:07:22,130
- What do I have to do to convince you, then?
- Marry Nana,

128
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:23,861
and I'll believe you!

129
00:07:26,959 --> 00:07:29,137
Yai! Don't you listen to me?!

130
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:33,533
- Somkuan, hurry!
- Yes, ma'am.

131
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,644
- That's enough.
- Yes.

132
00:07:35,644 --> 00:07:37,620
- Pack it up, quick!
- Yes, ma'am.

133
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:38,960
Go.

134
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,420
Hurry up.

135
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,377
Mom, Mom, Mom!

136
00:07:44,377 --> 00:07:46,200
You can't hit me like this!

137
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:49,400
- I'm not a child anymore.
- Why not? You're my son!

138
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,840
No matter how old you are, I can still hit you!

139
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,577
Ever since that woman entered your life,

140
00:07:53,577 --> 00:07:56,355
- you've always gone against me! Why?!
- Mom, Mom!

141
00:07:56,355 --> 00:08:00,420
Mom, listen!
I don't want to marry Nana right now

142
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,044
because it's not the right time.

143
00:08:02,044 --> 00:08:03,380
I still have work to do.

144
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:06,622
I don't have time, and I'm not in the mood
to be someone's husband.

145
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,100
Six months!

146
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,100
What did you say?

147
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,130
I'll give you six months

148
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:15,620
to finish all of your work!

149
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:18,000
And after that,

150
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:22,300
I'll talk to Nana's parents
to set the wedding date.

151
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:24,200
You have to do what I say.

152
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:13,360
Of course, you didn't notice when you came in

153
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:16,520
that I redecorated the stargazing spot for you.

154
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,820
You were angry,

155
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:22,680
and it blinded you.

156
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:24,044
Let me see

157
00:09:24,044 --> 00:09:26,622
where you're hurt
so I can dress your wounds. Come on.

158
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,200
Oh, I see one here. Lean this way.

159
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:31,220
It's going to sting.

160
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,820
Oh, dear.

161
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,300
<i>There's a nurse's office.</i>

162
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:51,511
<i>Why didn't you go there
and have them dress it?</i>

163
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,755
<i>They're heavy-handed.</i>

164
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,760
<i>I want you to do it for me</i>

165
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,755
<i>so I can look at you up close like this.</i>

166
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:04,240
<i>Ouch, Ran!</i>

167
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:06,400
<i>Oops, sorry.</i>

168
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:08,340
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

169
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:09,540
<i>I didn't mean to.</i>

170
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,580
<i>- It's okay.
- Oh.</i>

171
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:22,180
<i>Why is your mother so moody?</i>

172
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,900
<i>Does she do this to you often?</i>

173
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,022
<i>I'm used to it.</i>

174
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:30,840
<i>Why must you get used to it?</i>

175
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,800
<i>Why didn't you tell your grandmother
and father to protect you?</i>

176
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,860
<i>They never came to protect me in time.</i>

177
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:40,660
<i>My mom was always faster.</i>

178
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,220
<i>There's no changing her.</i>

179
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,980
<i>My parents never hit me or my siblings.</i>

180
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,620
<i>They love us so much.</i>

181
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:54,740
<i>Does your mother love you?</i>

182
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,526
<i>Hey, can you stop provoking me?</i>

183
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:16,860
<i>I have a business meeting.</i>

184
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:19,240
<i>And keep your voice down.</i>

185
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,400
<i>I don't want my mother and our son to hear it.</i>

186
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,222
<i>That's great!</i>

187
00:11:24,222 --> 00:11:26,755
<i>Now everyone will know
that you cheated on me!</i>

188
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:30,600
<i>I told you I have a business meeting!</i>

189
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,377
<i>Business meeting?!</i>

190
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,680
<i>A business meeting?!</i>

191
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:40,791
<i>Are you going to have a meeting
or look at that homewrecking bitch's boobs?!</i>

192
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:48,060
<i>Admit it! You cheated on me, didn't you?!</i>

193
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:49,911
<i>You dare hire a detective to follow me?!</i>

194
00:11:49,911 --> 00:11:51,466
<i>Yes!</i>

195
00:11:51,466 --> 00:11:54,622
<i>How else would I know
what a cheating husband I have?!</i>

196
00:11:54,622 --> 00:11:56,400
<i>Oh, like you're any better?!</i>

197
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:58,555
<i>You're truly horrible!</i>

198
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:04,660
<i>It's an adult problem.</i>

199
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:06,860
<i>Let them deal with it.</i>

200
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,700
<i>Don't dwell on it</i>

201
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:11,140
<i>and make yourself sad.</i>

202
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:15,288
<i>Grandma, can you make
my parents stop fighting?</i>

203
00:12:15,288 --> 00:12:18,577
<i>I want them to make up
and love each other like before.</i>

204
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:21,720
<i>I can only try to warn them,</i>

205
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:25,466
<i>but whether they'll come to their senses
and stop fighting,</i>

206
00:12:25,466 --> 00:12:27,100
<i>I have no idea.</i>

207
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,720
<i>You scumbag!</i>

208
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,200
<i>Bastard!</i>

209
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:55,420
<i>Mom.</i>

210
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:03,181
<i>Why do you have to look like your father?!</i>

211
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:07,020
<i>Why did you have to inherit his face?!</i>

212
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:08,644
<i>Why?!</i>

213
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:11,520
<i>I'm hurt...</i>

214
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,200
<i>You should be!</i>

215
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:16,260
<i>You must be hurt the same way
your father made me feel.</i>

216
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,460
<i>And you're useless now!</i>

217
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:24,080
<i>I want to give your father a son</i>

218
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,420
<i>so he will stop!</i>

219
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,540
<i>He never stops.</i>

220
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:33,280
<i>He's insatiable...</i>

221
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,820
<i>He never stops!</i>

222
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:37,133
<i>He never keeps his word!</i>

223
00:13:37,133 --> 00:13:40,080
<i>He never keeps his word!</i>

224
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,000
<i>Don't you love me anymore?</i>

225
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,933
<i>I hate you!</i>

226
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:48,300
<i>Don't you love me at all?</i>

227
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,622
<i>Of course, I do.</i>

228
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:11,222
<i>I love you, but...</i>

229
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,220
<i>But I'm angry.</i>

230
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,466
<i>Yai...</i>

231
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,533
<i>When you grow up,</i>

232
00:14:24,533 --> 00:14:26,420
<i>don't be like your father.</i>

233
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,888
<i>Don't hurt the woman who loves you</i>

234
00:14:29,888 --> 00:14:31,840
<i>and whom you love</i>

235
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:34,735
<i>the way I was hurt.</i>

236
00:14:34,735 --> 00:14:35,851
<i>I love you.</i>

237
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:38,311
<i>Ever since that day,</i>

238
00:14:38,311 --> 00:14:40,640
<i>I always let Mom take her anger out on me,</i>

239
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:44,666
<i>so when she's angry at my father,
she'll know that I'm still by her side</i>

240
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:47,140
<i>and that she's not all alone.</i>

241
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:51,620
<i>Are you crying?</i>

242
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:54,186
<i>No.</i>

243
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:58,280
<i>You can cry if you want to.</i>

244
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,760
<i>Cry with me.</i>

245
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:01,660
<i>I'll never make fun of you for it.</i>

246
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:06,980
<i>If you keep talking like that, I'll...</i>

247
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,365
<i>You're smiling now.</i>

248
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:14,740
<i>Thank you.</i>

249
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:17,780
<i>If you weren't this cheeky,</i>

250
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,360
<i>I wouldn't be able to smile.</i>

251
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,622
<i>Is it good?</i>

252
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:25,800
<i>It's very good.</i>

253
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:28,680
<i>Stay strong.</i>

254
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:30,740
<i>I'll make you smile every day.</i>

255
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,020
Do you really miss her?

256
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,680
Pardon?

257
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,777
You two were apart for more than ten years,

258
00:15:54,777 --> 00:15:56,420
then suddenly met again.

259
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,300
It must have happened for a reason.

260
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,320
Try to clear your mind

261
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,100
so you won't be blinded.

262
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,911
You can't let your mother
work hard like this anymore.

263
00:16:26,911 --> 00:16:29,688
You have to be especially cautious for now.

264
00:16:29,688 --> 00:16:31,533
Try to avoid the risk factors

265
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:33,155
that can trigger her condition.

266
00:16:33,155 --> 00:16:36,040
Your mother is also getting older.

267
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:39,420
Having frequent surgeries
is not good for her health.

268
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:41,040
Yes.

269
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:42,777
Thank you so much, sir.

270
00:16:42,777 --> 00:16:45,080
Also, don't forget to bring your mother in

271
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:47,360
for her follow-up appointment.

272
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,488
Yes.

273
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,688
Mom.

274
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:21,022
How are you feeling?

275
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,066
She's still dizzy from the anesthetic.

276
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,520
Did it hurt?

277
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:30,044
Of course it did.

278
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:35,700
I didn't know you had a spirit child, too.

279
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,200
Have you been fed?

280
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,200
Mom.

281
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:47,320
Do you want to move to a private room?

282
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:50,080
That way, I can stay with you all day.

283
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:53,020
The spirits can't answer this for you.

284
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:55,000
You'll have to answer it yourself.

285
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,340
It's okay.

286
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,880
It would waste so much money.

287
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,444
I'd rather stay in the general ward like this

288
00:18:02,444 --> 00:18:04,080
so I can be close to the nurses.

289
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:06,740
I'll also have people to talk to.

290
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,940
I still have the money I saved
to take care of you.

291
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,760
Keep it, my dear.

292
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:19,040
You'll need it for many other things, alright?

293
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:20,380
I can stay here.

294
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,640
The doctor said

295
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:27,120
you can't work hard anymore.

296
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:30,133
From now on, you have to
stop selling soybean milk

297
00:18:30,133 --> 00:18:32,600
and providing ironing services.

298
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:39,760
I'll hurry and find a job.

299
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:42,622
I'll find one that pays enough
to cover our expenses

300
00:18:42,622 --> 00:18:43,980
and support everyone.

301
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:57,360
While Mom is in the hospital,
I'll take care of her during the day.

302
00:18:57,360 --> 00:19:01,066
When visiting hours are over,
I'll go to job interviews and look for work.

303
00:19:01,066 --> 00:19:03,177
In the evening, Dao, you stay with Mom for me.

304
00:19:03,177 --> 00:19:06,000
You're no longer grounded. Stay here instead.

305
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,644
But if I'm free that day, you can just go home.

306
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:12,780
Okay, but...

307
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:14,660
Wait, what about Danai?

308
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,755
I have classes in the morning.

309
00:19:16,755 --> 00:19:18,577
In the evening, I have to work part-time.

310
00:19:18,577 --> 00:19:19,910
When can I even come?

311
00:19:19,910 --> 00:19:22,440
- No fair!
- I'm not finished.

312
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:24,422
As for Danai,
when you don't have morning classes,

313
00:19:24,422 --> 00:19:25,900
you have to take care of Mom.

314
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,533
But if none of us are available,

315
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:28,777
I'll ask the nurses,

316
00:19:28,777 --> 00:19:33,280
or maybe ask the family of the patient
in the next bed to look after her for us.

317
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,780
Would they be okay with that?

318
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:38,780
Why wouldn't they?
There's nothing wrong with being friendly.

319
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:40,160
Thai people are generous.

320
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:43,800
I'll buy them something to eat
to repay their kindness.

321
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:46,688
Come on. Let's go home,
or we'll go to bed too late.

322
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,022
<i>Don't forget</i>

323
00:20:27,022 --> 00:20:31,200
<i>to send me the names of
the Teacher's Day representatives.</i>

324
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:34,620
<i>Can I nominate someone now?</i>

325
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:36,760
<i>Who will you nominate?</i>

326
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,140
<i>Natasha and Rangsiman.</i>

327
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:43,111
<i>Representatives</i>

328
00:20:43,111 --> 00:20:45,860
<i>are supposed to be elected or appointed,</i>

329
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:48,700
<i>not nominated by just one person.</i>

330
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:52,266
<i>Everyone,</i>

331
00:20:52,266 --> 00:20:53,670
<i>which way do you prefer?</i>

332
00:20:53,670 --> 00:20:55,688
<i>- Election.
- Election.</i>

333
00:20:55,688 --> 00:20:56,933
<i>- Election.
- Election.</i>

334
00:20:56,933 --> 00:20:58,177
<i>Alright, okay.</i>

335
00:20:58,177 --> 00:21:00,155
<i>Then discuss it among yourselves first.</i>

336
00:21:00,155 --> 00:21:01,733
<i>Once you have the results,</i>

337
00:21:01,733 --> 00:21:04,900
<i>Natasha, submit the names to me.</i>

338
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:06,768
<i>Yes.</i>

339
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:17,180
[Natasha, Rangsiman]

340
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,866
<i>Would anyone like to object?</i>

341
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:23,911
<i>If no one objects, it means everyone agrees.</i>

342
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:54,333
<i>Does anyone want to nominate
someone else, hm?</i>

343
00:21:54,333 --> 00:21:57,090
<i>- Daran.
- Daran.</i>

344
00:21:57,090 --> 00:21:59,155
<i>Good, we have our female representative.</i>

345
00:21:59,155 --> 00:22:02,980
<i>Now, who should be the male representative?</i>

346
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,000
<i>Whoa!</i>

347
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:09,333
<i>Keep your hand raised.
Almost everyone in the room.</i>

348
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:12,755
<i>Keep your hand up. I can't choose.</i>

349
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:28,422
What're you dreaming about, dear?
You're even smiling.

350
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:31,540
Keep having sweet dreams.

351
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:37,220
Close the door.

352
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:59,580
- Go get Yai and tell him to come eat.
- Yes, ma'am.

353
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:00,660
Don't.

354
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,540
Let him rest.

355
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:06,560
He's an adult.

356
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:08,580
He can feed himself when he's hungry.

357
00:23:08,580 --> 00:23:10,960
Not having meals at the right time

358
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:13,640
can affect his health, Mother.

359
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:15,820
- Go get him!
- Yes, ma'am.

360
00:23:15,820 --> 00:23:17,140
Don't.

361
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,800
Yes, ma'am.

362
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:21,240
Go.

363
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,440
Yes?

364
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,890
Go stay out there.

365
00:23:23,890 --> 00:23:26,488
- Come inside when I call for you.
- Yes, ma'am.

366
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,860
I need to talk to you

367
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:40,180
about how you hurt Yai.

368
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:44,000
Did he tell you about that again?

369
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,080
What childish behavior!

370
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:48,377
Listen.

371
00:23:48,377 --> 00:23:51,355
Don't let me see or find out

372
00:23:51,355 --> 00:23:55,080
that you hurt Yai again like you always do.

373
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:57,180
I've been very patient with you.

374
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:02,060
- Yai doesn't have any problems with it--
- But I do!

375
00:24:02,060 --> 00:24:06,866
I've remained silent all this time
because Yai asked me to.

376
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:09,060
He loves his mother.

377
00:24:10,060 --> 00:24:12,940
But what kind of love is that
for your own child?

378
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:15,340
You see him as your enemy.

379
00:24:16,822 --> 00:24:18,160
Don't talk back.

380
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:21,960
Don't say that he reminds you of his father.

381
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:23,940
The husband that you hate so much

382
00:24:24,660 --> 00:24:26,160
has nothing to do with him.

383
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:28,720
If you want to punish
the one who wronged you.

384
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:29,920
Go!

385
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:31,580
Follow your husband to hell.

386
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:34,220
Go find him in hell!

387
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:38,980
I'm full.

388
00:24:38,980 --> 00:24:41,880
You'd better do as I say

389
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:44,911
if you still want to live in this house.

390
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:18,600
<i>Hello.</i>

391
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:19,920
<i>Hello.</i>

392
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:20,960
<i>I'm Alex,</i>

393
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:23,320
<i>a security guard at MJTV station.</i>

394
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:24,644
<i>Oh,</i>

395
00:25:24,644 --> 00:25:26,060
<i>you're the security guard.</i>

396
00:25:26,060 --> 00:25:29,400
The station is hiring new security guards.

397
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:31,288
The salary is 25,000 baht.

398
00:25:31,288 --> 00:25:33,360
Are you interested in applying?

399
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,880
What job was it again?

400
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:38,777
Security guard at MJTV station.

401
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:42,200
No, I'm not interested.

402
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:43,660
Thank you for calling me.

403
00:25:57,822 --> 00:25:59,980
25,000 baht.

404
00:25:59,980 --> 00:26:01,733
But I'll have to meet him...

405
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:04,620
25,000 baht...

406
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:08,228
I'll definitely see him.

407
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:12,200
Oh, 25,000 baht.

408
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:14,100
25,000 baht...

409
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:15,820
Hey!

410
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,111
Are you okay?

411
00:26:55,640 --> 00:26:58,711
The security building is this way.
I'll take you there.

412
00:27:13,320 --> 00:27:14,422
Dad.

413
00:27:14,422 --> 00:27:15,600
"Chief."

414
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:16,720
Chief Dad.

415
00:27:16,720 --> 00:27:18,640
Chief Dad, my ass!

416
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:21,640
Isn't it true? You're both my dad and my chief.

417
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,800
Jeez, you're such a...

418
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:25,803
Do you have a thick skull?

419
00:27:25,803 --> 00:27:27,384
You never remember what I told you.

420
00:27:27,384 --> 00:27:30,244
On the job, don't call me "Dad"!

421
00:27:30,244 --> 00:27:31,500
Call me "Chief"!

422
00:27:31,500 --> 00:27:34,111
- Yes, Chief!
- What is it?

423
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:37,733
Is that Mr. Alex's girlfriend?
He gets so close to her.

424
00:27:37,733 --> 00:27:39,340
He has never done this to anyone.

425
00:27:39,340 --> 00:27:41,680
Ask him. I have no idea.

426
00:27:41,680 --> 00:27:43,920
- Okay.
- Hey.

427
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:45,900
- Where are you going?
- I'm going to ask him.

428
00:27:45,900 --> 00:27:48,220
Oh, Boy!

429
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:51,700
I mean... I'll smack you!

430
00:27:51,700 --> 00:27:53,340
I mean,

431
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:56,880
ask him privately, not right now!

432
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:59,720
- I'll ask him later, then.
- I'm going to fire you!

433
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:05,340
The next step is an interview
with Uncle Narong.

434
00:28:07,044 --> 00:28:08,422
I'm going on patrol now.

435
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:10,244
Okay.

436
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:20,160
Boy, let's go.

437
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:21,266
Yes.

438
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:41,711
Are you not going to look at
my application form and work history?

439
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:45,333
Oh.

440
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:50,160
I was trying to get my brain working.

441
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:52,111
Application form...

442
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:56,066
Oh, taekwondo...

443
00:28:56,066 --> 00:28:57,666
Excellent!

444
00:28:57,666 --> 00:29:02,244
You have taekwondo skills!
Excellent. You're hired!

445
00:29:02,244 --> 00:29:03,288
Yes?

446
00:29:03,288 --> 00:29:05,000
Is that your girlfriend, Mr. Alex?

447
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:08,600
Are you crazy? She's not my girlfriend
but an angel.

448
00:29:09,936 --> 00:29:11,160
Follow me.

449
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:13,252
Don't you want to know
why I called her "Angel"?

450
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:16,870
Of course I do. Who is she?

451
00:29:16,870 --> 00:29:18,377
Who is she?

452
00:29:18,377 --> 00:29:21,110
Well... We're urgently seeking new employees.

453
00:29:21,110 --> 00:29:25,800
But most importantly,
you have taekwondo skills,

454
00:29:25,800 --> 00:29:29,780
which makes you a great fit
for our security team.

455
00:29:29,780 --> 00:29:31,240
You're hired now.

456
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:33,733
- Really?
- Yes.

457
00:29:33,733 --> 00:29:35,288
Don't overthink it.

458
00:29:35,288 --> 00:29:38,133
The salary is just as Mr. Alex told you.

459
00:29:38,133 --> 00:29:40,044
The probation period is three months.

460
00:29:40,044 --> 00:29:43,704
Another thing is that you can move
into the security guards' dormitory

461
00:29:43,704 --> 00:29:45,360
we've prepared for you.

462
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:48,413
This is one of the benefits for our employees.

463
00:29:48,413 --> 00:29:50,407
Okay? You can start tomorrow.

464
00:29:50,407 --> 00:29:51,952
Yes?

465
00:29:51,952 --> 00:29:53,640
Is there anything wrong?

466
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:55,040
Oh...

467
00:29:55,040 --> 00:29:58,720
- Thank you, Chief, for accepting me.
- Alright. Good.

468
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:00,789
- I'm okay with everything.
- That's good.

469
00:30:00,789 --> 00:30:03,870
But except for one thing.

470
00:30:03,870 --> 00:30:06,980
Can I wait until my mother
is discharged from the hospital

471
00:30:06,980 --> 00:30:08,200
before I start working?

472
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,911
Start whenever you can.

473
00:30:09,911 --> 00:30:11,644
Wouldn't that be too late?

474
00:30:11,644 --> 00:30:13,730
I thought you said you were short-staffed.

475
00:30:13,730 --> 00:30:15,333
Oh, not at all.

476
00:30:15,333 --> 00:30:16,888
We're always hiring.

477
00:30:16,888 --> 00:30:20,133
So if someone applies,
we'll let them start right away,

478
00:30:20,133 --> 00:30:23,440
and you can take care of your mother first.

479
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:25,400
Start whenever you're ready.

480
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:28,800
- Thank you so much, Chief.
- Yes, yes, yes.

481
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:34,820
[Chief's Office]
[Security Department]

482
00:30:37,420 --> 00:30:40,780
[Security Office Department]

483
00:30:41,360 --> 00:30:42,700
Hello.

484
00:30:42,700 --> 00:30:44,680
I've hired her.

485
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:47,720
She said she'd like to start

486
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,933
after her mother is discharged
from the hospital.

487
00:30:50,520 --> 00:30:52,377
"Keep the documents"?

488
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:56,488
Don't upload them into the system?

489
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:00,960
Okay, sir.

490
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:02,044
Yes.

491
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:37,400
If it's too much, you can come home, okay?

492
00:31:38,040 --> 00:31:39,866
Yeah, call me right away

493
00:31:39,866 --> 00:31:41,560
- so I can go pick you up.
- Yes.

494
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:43,755
We don't have much choice at this point.

495
00:31:43,755 --> 00:31:45,222
I have to do it.

496
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:49,022
Why is everyone talking as if
she is going off to war?

497
00:31:49,022 --> 00:31:52,720
Well, being a security guard
is like being a soldier, isn't it?

498
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:54,480
It's a dangerous job.

499
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:56,320
The people in the TV station building

500
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:59,160
won't be dangerous enough to harm her.

501
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:03,288
Even if there are, they won't stand a chance
against your demon-slaying kick.

502
00:32:03,288 --> 00:32:05,000
You're amazing, aren't you?

503
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:06,480
Yes, I am.

504
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:08,520
Wow, what a self-assured person.

505
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:10,860
It's called boosting one's morale.

506
00:32:11,700 --> 00:32:14,400
Then can I go see you?

507
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:16,222
- No!
- No!

508
00:32:16,222 --> 00:32:18,700
Why did you all say that in perfect sync?!

509
00:32:18,700 --> 00:32:20,640
You just want to meet your bias.

510
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:23,777
Mom, look at Dao,
she's planning to skip class again.

511
00:32:23,777 --> 00:32:25,066
No, don't do that.

512
00:32:25,066 --> 00:32:27,266
I can go outside of school time, Danai!

513
00:32:27,266 --> 00:32:30,080
You have to keep Mom company
since I'm not home.

514
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:31,177
Fine.

515
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:41,800
After the incident involving
the "Cutie Sam Sweety Nut" fandom,

516
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:45,480
whose members urged us to consider
their feelings, their affection,

517
00:32:45,480 --> 00:32:48,380
and the bond they have with the two idols

518
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:51,560
while they work together as a pair,

519
00:32:51,560 --> 00:32:55,080
it was one of the most heartfelt things
I've ever heard.

520
00:32:55,080 --> 00:32:58,600
So I've decided to honor those feelings.

521
00:32:59,680 --> 00:33:01,040
Please come in.

522
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:05,180
Hey, Luknut is here!

523
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,600
Glad to see you again.

524
00:33:09,600 --> 00:33:11,180
Thank you.

525
00:33:11,180 --> 00:33:12,534
- Wow!
- Sam!

526
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:16,060
Move your head closer, do it for me, please.

527
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:22,244
My shipper wish is fulfilled.

528
00:33:22,244 --> 00:33:23,288
Incredible!

529
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:40,160
Yai!

530
00:33:41,112 --> 00:33:43,320
I'll talk to you later.

531
00:33:43,320 --> 00:33:47,280
Thank you again for allowing
Luknut to work with us.

532
00:33:47,280 --> 00:33:48,500
Thank you so much.

533
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:52,355
You're not going to tell me
anything about this?

534
00:33:52,355 --> 00:33:55,355
You suddenly dropped my male lead
and replaced him with Luknut like this?

535
00:33:55,355 --> 00:33:57,800
I'm the producer who works on this project.

536
00:33:57,800 --> 00:33:59,320
This is so disrespectful.

537
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:01,760
You wouldn't listen to me even if I told you.

538
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:03,780
So this is the best method.

539
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:06,320
So cold,

540
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:07,760
both toward our work

541
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:09,800
and our relationship.

542
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:11,920
Which topic would you like to discuss first?

543
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:14,220
Work or personal matters?

544
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:18,516
Both.

545
00:34:18,516 --> 00:34:19,822
Aren't you afraid at all

546
00:34:19,822 --> 00:34:22,620
that I might tell my father to
withdraw his shares from the company?

547
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:26,933
Or would you rather I break off
the engagement first?

548
00:34:26,933 --> 00:34:28,560
I'm not scared.

549
00:34:28,560 --> 00:34:29,694
I'm waiting for it.

550
00:34:30,780 --> 00:34:32,280
Yai.

551
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:33,460
When will that be?

552
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:40,880
Better not, then.

553
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:44,525
I'll just leave things as messy as they are.

554
00:34:44,525 --> 00:34:46,970
Because whatever you plan to do,

555
00:34:46,970 --> 00:34:50,120
I'll just keep being a thorn in your side

556
00:34:50,120 --> 00:34:52,800
until you finally give up.

557
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:55,000
Because I'll be the victor

558
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:57,520
in everything.

559
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:24,520
<i>After the incident involving
the "Cutie Sam Sweety Nut" fandom,</i>

560
00:35:24,520 --> 00:35:28,480
<i>whose members urged us to consider
their feelings, their affection,</i>

561
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:31,680
<i>So I've decided to honor those feelings.</i>

562
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,111
<i>Please come in.</i>

563
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:43,386
Dao, keep it down.
I'm talking to my girlfriend!

564
00:35:52,669 --> 00:35:53,825
Ran,

565
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:56,660
will you be alright?

566
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:00,940
I'll be fine, Mom.

567
00:36:02,937 --> 00:36:05,317
The only thing I care about right now is money.

568
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,460
What will you do if you meet him?

569
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,622
It can't be helped.

570
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,740
I'll just fulfill my duty as best as I can.

571
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:23,300
I won't let him hurt me
to the point I have to leave this job.

572
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,800
Oh, Ran...

573
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,740
If I could help you,

574
00:36:27,740 --> 00:36:29,940
you wouldn't have to do this.

575
00:36:32,540 --> 00:36:35,480
I have to take responsibility
for my own life, Mom.

576
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:37,260
I'll choose my own path.

577
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:39,800
So...

578
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:42,266
Whatever life has in store for me,

579
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,980
I'll have to get through it.

580
00:36:48,720 --> 00:36:50,977
May blessings be with you.

581
00:36:50,977 --> 00:36:52,444
I wish you safety,

582
00:36:52,444 --> 00:36:54,933
and may you be protected from
those who wish you harm.

583
00:36:57,111 --> 00:36:58,622
Thank you, Mom.

584
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:03,180
Thank you for being
my moral support this entire time.

585
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:08,560
Ran, Ran!

586
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,968
- Dao.
- That old chump listened to me!

587
00:37:10,968 --> 00:37:13,948
What is it? Take it easy. Easy.

588
00:37:14,640 --> 00:37:15,844
Ran.

589
00:37:15,844 --> 00:37:17,020
Okay,

590
00:37:17,020 --> 00:37:19,244
I'll leave you two to it.

591
00:37:19,244 --> 00:37:22,200
It's going to be a while
before you see her again.

592
00:37:22,200 --> 00:37:23,900
I'll go to sleep now, okay?

593
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:29,100
Go ahead, talk, talk.

594
00:37:29,100 --> 00:37:31,440
- I'll leave now.
- Can you stand?

595
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,780
Not really.

596
00:37:34,480 --> 00:37:36,644
Hey, Ran, look.

597
00:37:36,644 --> 00:37:38,555
Do you see this? Look!

598
00:37:49,380 --> 00:37:51,680
<i>We aren't some generic, senseless fans.</i>

599
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:54,507
<i>We've already seen
Sam at an event with Pangya,</i>

600
00:37:54,507 --> 00:37:56,320
<i>and we found that</i>

601
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:59,500
<i>it won't work!</i>

602
00:38:11,380 --> 00:38:12,955
You rascal.

603
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:16,700
Do you know what I had to go through?

604
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:27,644
Actually...

605
00:38:27,644 --> 00:38:29,720
That old chump is pretty nice.

606
00:38:29,720 --> 00:38:32,000
He listened to a kid like me.

607
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,950
He listened to the fans

608
00:38:33,950 --> 00:38:36,260
instead of acting all conceited.

609
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:39,980
I feel bad for scolding him.

610
00:38:39,980 --> 00:38:42,040
Should I go apologize?

611
00:38:42,040 --> 00:38:43,480
No.

612
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:45,120
Why?

613
00:38:45,120 --> 00:38:46,680
Well...

614
00:38:46,680 --> 00:38:48,466
It's enough already.

615
00:38:48,466 --> 00:38:51,640
If you do any more, he might get annoyed.

616
00:38:51,640 --> 00:38:53,740
You're right.

617
00:38:53,740 --> 00:38:54,860
Then...

618
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:58,700
Can I ask you to get
Sam and Luknut's signatures?

619
00:38:58,700 --> 00:39:00,820
I will if I get the chance.

620
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:03,620
Thank you so much.

621
00:39:04,400 --> 00:39:06,133
You care so much about your idols.

622
00:39:06,133 --> 00:39:07,740
Be careful. Your grades might slip.

623
00:39:07,740 --> 00:39:11,040
Well, you don't have to worry.

624
00:39:11,040 --> 00:39:13,120
What GPA did you get this semester?

625
00:39:13,120 --> 00:39:15,044
3.85.

626
00:39:15,044 --> 00:39:18,244
My math teacher didn't give me all my points.

627
00:39:18,244 --> 00:39:20,555
When I questioned it, he said,

628
00:39:20,555 --> 00:39:23,240
"The answer is correct,
but the method is wrong."

629
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:26,733
How could it be wrong
if I got the right answer?

630
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:32,444
Please don't nag me
about my grades dropping, alright?

631
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:40,700
You're staying in a dorm

632
00:39:40,700 --> 00:39:43,160
and can only come home on your days off.

633
00:39:43,160 --> 00:39:45,733
That means I won't have anyone
to stargaze with.

634
00:39:47,120 --> 00:39:49,000
You can call me.

635
00:39:49,000 --> 00:39:50,900
I'll look at the stars there,

636
00:39:50,900 --> 00:39:52,380
while you do that here.

637
00:39:52,380 --> 00:39:55,688
That way, we can stargaze together, okay?

638
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:07,760
<i>♪ If you're a mountain, then I'll be a forest ♪</i>

639
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:12,540
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you warm in my chest ♪</i>

640
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:19,200
<i>♪ If you're the sky, then I'll be the clouds ♪</i>

641
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:23,600
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you company ♪</i>

642
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:27,911
<i>♪ If you're a car, then I'll be the roads ♪</i>

643
00:40:27,911 --> 00:40:32,040
<i>♪ If you're the Moon,
then I'll be the stars for you ♪</i>

644
00:40:32,040 --> 00:40:36,555
<i>♪ Staying by your side and giving you warmth ♪</i>

645
00:40:36,555 --> 00:40:40,420
<i>♪ Even when you're down,
I won't leave your side ♪</i>

646
00:40:47,300 --> 00:40:48,980
<i>I want to stay like this forever.</i>

647
00:40:51,040 --> 00:40:52,540
<i>Me too.</i>

648
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:56,377
<i>I love you the most.</i>

649
00:40:57,420 --> 00:40:59,340
<i>I love you the most too.</i>

650
00:41:50,740 --> 00:41:52,180
"Love the most"?

651
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:36,733
I'll have Boy get your uniform,

652
00:42:36,733 --> 00:42:39,120
then have him show you to your room.

653
00:42:39,120 --> 00:42:43,120
Rest well and relax.
Then start working tomorrow.

654
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:45,840
Yes, thank you so much, Chief.

655
00:42:45,840 --> 00:42:47,422
Whoa, no need to be so formal.

656
00:42:47,422 --> 00:42:49,640
Hey, Boy. Do your job.

657
00:42:49,640 --> 00:42:51,260
Yes, Chief.

658
00:42:53,460 --> 00:42:55,622
Please follow me, Ms. Daran.

659
00:42:56,380 --> 00:42:58,140
Alright.

660
00:43:01,960 --> 00:43:04,080
The security guard dormitory is at the back.

661
00:43:04,080 --> 00:43:05,675
Just go straight, and you'll get there.

662
00:43:15,760 --> 00:43:17,280
Hello?

663
00:43:17,280 --> 00:43:19,577
I've arrived. I'll be there soon.

664
00:43:19,577 --> 00:43:20,622
Yes.

665
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:31,600
All the other floors are full.

666
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:33,640
Your room is on the top floor.

667
00:43:33,640 --> 00:43:34,920
It's a penthouse.

668
00:43:34,920 --> 00:43:36,760
A penthouse?

669
00:43:36,760 --> 00:43:38,720
I'm just exaggerating.

670
00:43:38,720 --> 00:43:42,711
There's only one other resident
in the penthouse, and that's Alex.

671
00:43:44,720 --> 00:43:46,511
Oh, don't worry.

672
00:43:46,511 --> 00:43:49,440
He's gay, so you're completely safe.

673
00:43:51,120 --> 00:43:53,840
But you don't have to call me Miss.

674
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,160
I'm not used to that.

675
00:43:55,160 --> 00:43:58,111
Since we're coworkers,
there's no need to be so formal.

676
00:43:58,111 --> 00:43:59,800
How does that sound?

677
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:01,040
Sounds great.

678
00:44:01,040 --> 00:44:03,520
Because I feel so tense!

679
00:44:03,520 --> 00:44:04,845
Why?

680
00:44:05,820 --> 00:44:07,000
It's nothing.

681
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:09,222
I'll call you like Mr. Alex,

682
00:44:10,120 --> 00:44:11,377
like Alex calls you.

683
00:44:11,377 --> 00:44:13,222
Can I call you Ran?

684
00:44:13,222 --> 00:44:16,111
Of course, Boy.

685
00:44:16,111 --> 00:44:18,022
Just a bit more and we'll be there.

686
00:44:22,488 --> 00:44:25,700
Hello, I'm Narong from the Security Department.

687
00:44:25,700 --> 00:44:27,140
Uncle Narong, it's me.

688
00:44:27,840 --> 00:44:30,320
Can I have the files on
the new security guards?

689
00:44:30,320 --> 00:44:32,980
Yes. Of course.

690
00:44:42,160 --> 00:44:44,765
You've got the layout down now, right?

691
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:45,792
Yes.

692
00:44:45,792 --> 00:44:48,915
Good. I'll take you
to your assigned post, then.

693
00:44:48,915 --> 00:44:50,350
- Yes.
- This way.

694
00:45:20,520 --> 00:45:23,977
<i>Your minimart zombie girl
works as a security guard here?</i>

695
00:45:23,977 --> 00:45:25,696
<i>Can you take care of her for me?</i>

696
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:27,938
<i>That zombie girl.</i>

697
00:45:28,680 --> 00:45:30,666
<i>You seem well-educated.</i>

698
00:45:30,666 --> 00:45:32,579
<i>You shouldn't be working as a guard.</i>

699
00:45:33,440 --> 00:45:35,000
<i>Eat lots and lots, okay?</i>

700
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,480
<i>You look too thin.</i>

701
00:45:36,480 --> 00:45:37,644
<i>I am?</i>

702
00:45:37,644 --> 00:45:40,800
<i>I get off work quite late,
so I'll see you at the building tomorrow.</i>

703
00:45:40,800 --> 00:45:42,133
<i>How sweet.</i>

704
00:45:42,133 --> 00:45:44,760
<i>She is Yai's ex, you fool.</i>

705
00:45:44,760 --> 00:45:45,866
<i>What?</i>

706
00:45:45,866 --> 00:45:48,644
<i>Are you trying to rekindle an old flame?</i>
